<article class="env-lemma" id="00PF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00PF">Lemma <span data-tag="00PF">10.119.11</span>.</a> Let $R$ be a domain with fraction field $K$. Let $M$ be an $R$-submodule of $K^{\oplus r}$. Assume $R$ is Noetherian of dimension $1$. For any nonzero $x \in R$ we have $\text{length}_ R(M/xM) < \infty $. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since $R$ has dimension $1$ we see that $x$ is contained in finitely many primes $\mathfrak m_ i$, $i = 1, \ldots , n$, each maximal. Since $R$ is Noetherian we see that $R/xR$ is Artinian and $R/xR = \prod _{i = 1, \ldots , n} (R/xR)_{\mathfrak m_ i}$ by Proposition <a href="/tag/00KJ" data-tag="00KJ">10.60.7</a> and Lemma <a href="/tag/00JB" data-tag="00JB">10.53.6</a>. Hence $M/xM$ similarly decomposes as the product $M/xM = \prod (M/xM)_{\mathfrak m_ i}$ of its localizations at the $\mathfrak m_ i$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/00PE" data-tag="00PE">10.119.9</a> applied to $M_{\mathfrak m_ i}$ over $R_{\mathfrak m_ i}$ we see each $M_{\mathfrak m_ i}/xM_{\mathfrak m_ i} = (M/xM)_{\mathfrak m_ i}$ has finite length over $R_{\mathfrak m_ i}$. Thus $M/xM$ has finite length over $R$ as the above implies $M/xM$ has a finite filtration by $R$-submodules whose successive quotients are isomorphic to the residue fields $\kappa (\mathfrak m_ i)$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>